        "manufacturing_body": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Everything is made in London, by two women-led studios we work with closely.</p><p>Our toiles come from a sampling studio that works almost entirely in deadstock. Sampling is where a lot of fashion's quiet waste happens: a piece goes through several versions before it's right, and all of that fabric is usually thrown away. Working with deadstock gives abandoned fabrics a new purpose, costing the planet nothing new thus reducing waste.</p><p>The garments themselves are made in a factory that holds SMETA and Fast Forward ethical audits. They also run a training academy in garment skills with apprenticeships and qualifications up to degree level, and houses a repair centre that employs and trains people who find it hard to get work, including people from refugee backgrounds.</p><p>We're small enough to know the people making our clothes and to be in the room while they're being made. Small runs mean nobody is rushed, and you can see that in our quality.</p>",
            "width": "100%",
            "max_width": "none",
            "alignment": "left",
