        "fabrics_body": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Most of our fabrics are sourced locally and deadstock — mill ends, cancelled orders, rolls left behind by houses that over-ordered. When we do buy new, it's natural fibre. Either way it has to be good: we're making things meant to last ten years.</p><p>And the clothes are only part of it. We're working towards workshops for sewing, mending, pattern cutting, and open evenings where people can bring their own projects and sit at the same table. Learning to make and repair things is the other half of buying less.</p>",
